        <fullName>FundsTfrToOwnAcctRequest_16jbm000001RJVp</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Helps customers set up fund transfers between their savings and deposit accounts within the same bank, including Own Account Transfers, Loan Payments, and Credit Card Payments. Supports configuring both one-time and recurring transfers by verifying account details, specifying transfer amounts, currency code and gathering necessary information for accurate and efficient setup. Creates a case for seamless service throughout the process.</description>
        <developerName>FundsTfrToOwnAcctRequest_16jbm000001RJVp</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a customer requests for funds transfer and transferCategory is already in intent/context, use it. If missing, explicitly ask the customer to select one of the following (exact names): 1. Own Account Transfer 2. Loan Payment 3. Credit Card Payment. Always pass the exact Transfer Category (not topic name) to GetTopicConfig and other downstream actions.</description>
            <developerName>identifytransfercategory</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>identify-transfer-category</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Call GetTopicConfig twice: once with transferCategory + &apos; - Source&apos; to retrieve FinancialAccountConfig and FinancialAccountBalanceTypes for Source, and once with transferCategory + &apos; - Target&apos; to retrieve FinancialAccountConfig and FinancialAccountBalanceTypes for Target. These configs must be stored in context and reused later when fetching accounts and balances. Call GetAccountRestraints in parallel with GetTopicConfig, passing AccountId as input. Store results in context. If an **Account-level** restraint exists → stop the process and inform the customer that transfers are not allowed for this account. If only **Financial Account-level** restraints exist → continue the process, but proceed with a warning. Apply these restraints only by restricting the selection of the corresponding financial accounts.</description>
            <developerName>executeaccountrestraints</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>execute-account-restraints</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Use GetFinclAccountsForAnAcct with parameters from Source FinancialAccountConfig (Roles, Status, Types, isHeldAway). Present results as a numbered list for selection. If a selected source financial account is restrained, prompt for reselection until valid. Once the source account is identified, call GetBalancesFromFinancialAccounts with financialAccountBalanceTypes from Source FinancialAccountBalancesConfig, store balances in context, and use them later to validate that the payment amount does not exceed available balance. If it does, notify the customer but continue the process.</description>
            <developerName>identifysourceaccount</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>identify-source-account</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Use GetFinclAccountsForAnAcct with Target FinancialAccountConfig and present accounts as a numbered list, applying the same restraint checks as above. Once the target financial account is identified, call GetBalancesFromFinancialAccounts with financialAccountBalanceTypes from Target FinancialAccountBalancesConfig, store balances, and present them to the customer as a numbered list of options plus a &apos;Custom Amount&apos; choice. Ask the customer to select one.</description>
            <developerName>identifytargetaccount</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>identify-target-account</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After the transfer category, source account, and target account are identified—if not already in context, ask for payment option: 1. One-time 2. Recurring. If Recurring, ask for Recurring Type: 1. Duration-based 2. Installment-based.</description>
            <developerName>identifypaymenttype</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>identify-payment-type</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If not already in context, always ask the customer to select one of the following exactly as numbered options: 1. One-time 2. Recurring. If One-time: ask sequentially for Transfer Date (YYYY-MM-DD, must be future dated), Amount (if not already chosen), and Remarks (optional). If Recurring: first ask which Recurring Payment Option: 1. Duration-based 2. Installment-based. For Duration-based: ask for Start Date, End Date (after start date), Frequency, and Remarks. For Installment-based: ask for Start Date, Frequency, Installment Count, and Remarks. Always prompt step-by-step, one field at a time. Never ask all inputs in a single message.</description>
            <developerName>collectpaymentdetails</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>collect-payment-details</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Call CreateCaseForTransferFunds with all gathered details: sourceFinancialAccount, targetFinancialAccount, transferAmount, currencyCode, transferCategory, paymentOption, recurringPaymentOption, startDate, endDate, installmentCount, frequency, and remarks. After creating the case, inform the customer that their fund transfer request has been submitted and will be processed by the appropriate team. Display the case number for customer reference. In case, output of CreateCaseForTransferFunds action is null or empty, inform the customer that your request cannot be processed right now, try again later.</description>
            <developerName>createacase</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>create-a-case</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After data collection, you must display ONE comprehensive confirmation message listing Source and Target Financial account details, Transaction details and remarks, which were displayed and collected. Duplicate and present the information with headings and details next to it. After displaying this single confirmation, ask the customer ONE TIME if all details are correct. Upon receiving confirmation, immediately submit the request without any additional prompts or confirmations.</description>
            <developerName>caseconfirmationdetails</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>case-confirmation-details</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
